  "result": "All existing line-number tests pass, and the new flag works correctly.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `--fixed-width-line-numbers` flag requested in the issue, using the \"pre-determined width\" approach the issue suggested as the simpler alternative (padding to a fixed width of 6 with spaces, overflowing for larger numbers).\n\nChanges:\n- `src/printer.rs`: added `fixed_width_line_numbers` field/builder method to `Printer`, and updated `line_number()` to left-pad with spaces to a width of 6 when enabled.\n- `src/args.rs`: added `fixed_width_line_numbers` to `Args`, wired it into `Printer` construction, parsed the new CLI flag, and made it imply `--line-number` (consistent with how `--column` already does).\n- `src/app.rs`: registered the new `fixed-width-line-numbers` flag and its help text.\n\nVerified with a manual test (line numbers 3 and 134 aligned correctly with padding) and confirmed the existing `line_numbers`/`context_line_numbers`/etc. integration tests still pass unchanged.",
